From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:43:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dynamic word-timed captions for topic videos (short-form
 social style)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A1 item from the open-source study: captions that pop in big 2-3 word
groups in sync with the narration — the style every high-performing
short-form video uses — next to the existing classic sentence subtitles.

- wordTimings.ts: per-word timing WITHOUT a transcription model. Every
  sentence's boundaries are already measured exactly (per-sentence TTS with
  WAV-header timing), so distributing each sentence's duration across its
  words proportionally to length lands within a frame or two of the voice.
  Deterministic, zero extra AI cost. CJK runs split into 4-char groups so
  the style works in every script.
- buildCaptionChunks(): groups words into <=3-word / ~16-char captions that
  never cross a sentence boundary; each holds until the next appears.
- compose.ts: captionStyle "classic" | "dynamic". Dynamic renders bigger
  type (h/13), heavier stroke, positioned at the short-form focal point
  (72% height), one drawtext per chunk via the existing textfile mechanism.
- Contract: GenerateVideo captionStyle enum + VideoJobOptions.captionStyle;
  studio offers Dynamic (default for new videos) / Classic under the
  subtitles switch.

Verified: 62 topicVideo+routes tests green (incl. a real-ffmpeg dynamic
render), 12 studio page tests, root typecheck, spec lint, codegen committed.

